{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Its feet.</b> I searched all of Scripture and found no instance where פעם means corners, but only from the root meaning foot: \"the feet of the poor, the steps of the needy\" (Isaiah 26:6); \"and set [them] on the path of his feet\" (Psalms 85:14 [n]); \"How beautiful are your feet\" (Song of Songs 7:2), and many like these. Therefore I was compelled to explain that the ark had feet, for it would be dishonorable for the ark to rest on the ground. Furthermore, what reason is there to say, \"and two gold rings,\" with the added vav — for if these were the first ones, it should have been written \"two rings,\" to make known that they are four gold rings, as he mentioned, in accordance with the usage of the language. There are some of the scholars of our generation who understood this, and said that the poles were placed in the ark through rings that were on the feet, and when they needed to carry the ark, they would be removed from the lower rings and placed in the upper rings. And thus it is written, \"and they shall put its poles\" (Numbers 4:6). In my opinion, the poles, once they were placed in the upper rings, were not removed from there, for thus it is written, \"they shall not be removed from it\" (below, verse 15). And the meaning of \"and they shall put its poles\" refers to the priests, who would place the poles of the ark on the shoulders of the Kohathites. And when the ark was set in the shrine, because it was adjacent to the wall, so that the cherubim were spread over the ark and over its poles, therefore the end of each of the poles was lengthened — and this is \"and the poles were lengthened\" (1 Kings 8:8). Now the four lower rings were for beauty and splendor, as is the manner of chests."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Psalms 85:14; the Hebrew text gives תה' פה י\"ד (= 85:14), correct as rendered."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:20.225461983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}